An `Error` carries a message and an unsigned numeric code.

[codeblock, $code("moth"):
    missing = Error("Missing value")
    coded = Error("Missing value", 200)
]

The code defaults to `0` and accepts `0` through `4294967295`. A negative code is
rejected, and an `Int` variable needs an explicit conversion.

Use the message to explain the failure. Use the code when a stable category is
useful to callers or tools.

The compiler and HTML-JS backend support this `U32` contract. HTML-Wasm still
rejects reachable `Error` values. See @../progress (Progress) for backend support.
